BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Big Questions' Special Talk Series: AI & The Soul
DTSTART:20261030T230000Z
DTEND:20261031T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T123107Z
UID:localist-54348151178916-54348151179941@ucsd-grad-calendar
CATEGORIES:ISEO (iEvents)
DESCRIPTION:Are we defined by silicon or something far greater? Delving in
 to the deep-seated anxieties of "Why AI Haunts Us" and the hardware bounda
 ries defined in "The Limits of Silicon"\, this presentation unpacks what t
 echnology can and cannot achieve. The talk then elevates the conversation 
 by contrasting "Derived vs Inherent Value" and grounding our true signific
 ance in the foundational idea that "God the Creator Gives Worth". Join us 
 for a punchy\, thought-provoking look at the real limits of tech and where
  our value truly lies!\n\nSource: ISEO (iEvents)\n\nhttps://calendar.ucsd.
 edu/event/the-big-questions-special-talk-series-ai-the-soul
LOCATION:Dirty Birds @ Price Center
URL:https://calendar.ucsd.edu/event/the-big-questions-special-talk-series-
 ai-the-soul
END:VEVENT
